29,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings are concerning. The late-turn pool is depleted, and we are relying on overtime for both final departures and overnight maintenance. We are stretched thin.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Interestingly, the mid-city runs are slower than they used to be, but the crowds clear at the same rate. The delay isn't the crowd; it's the transit time.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The financial picture is fragmented. We have a lapsed grant balance, but our operating and technology budgets have been trimmed. Contractor fees are eating our paving budget.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Servas,,"History provides a glimmer of hope. A late-evening pilot from eight years ago met its cost-recovery targets, and some accessibility rebuilds were completed successfully.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ground is treacherous. Pre-war shells have unrecorded voids causing weeks of delays, and the ferry and rail offices cannot even agree on passenger data terms.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if the late-evening pilot worked, we must ask if we still have the staff to support it. My data suggests we do not.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, if the technology budget is trimmed, can we even afford a new fare system? I found that passengers aren't waiting at machines; the delay is in the journey.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, a fair point. The technology line is indeed lean. We must be careful not to commit to a system that requires ongoing high-cost contractor fees.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you are right to be cautious. However, the success of the past shows the demand exists. We must find a way to balance ambition with capacity.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Asuka, the maintenance crews are also a factor. If we choose a plan involving old stations, the ""unrecorded voids"" I found will likely stall everything.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, exactly. Any plan requiring heavy physical work in old shells or more late-night staffing is a risk to the few crews we have left.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"It seems we should avoid things that just ""look"" crowded and focus on the actual transit time or the systemic bottlenecks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. We need a solution that doesn't create a permanent financial drain or rely on a budget line that is currently being trimmed.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We are uncovering the friction points. We need a plan that is historically viable, financially sustainable, and operationally possible.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,And one that doesn't require a miracle of cooperation between agencies that can't even agree on data terms.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
